Notebook[{
Cell["Hypermatrix", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"6434c34e-32fe-7046-a112-62bbaef25d03"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c07ca0ed-2504-f54d-8d50-ee3dedefbcdc"],
 " ",
 "represents the given arrays as a hypermatrix, holding them in canonical \
order."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"65718102-fad0-3a49-8324-d99362a7c542"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ab52e00b-0c60-bc43-b78c-16f38796dc42"],
 " ",
 "is equivalent."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"679d7904-3cf9-5e4d-82ab-999c198bb726"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"3048dc9e-fccf-4343-83a1-267edfbadf75"],

Cell["\<\
The arrays are ordered by array order, lowest first; then by dimensions, \
shorter first, compared term by term; then by symmetry, taking \"Symmetric\" \
before \"Cyclic\" before \"Rigid\".\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b88d6314-873e-2742-8000-b422f0c264c3"],

Cell["\<\
Two arrays alike in all three are put in the Wolfram Language's own canonical \
order, so that a hypermatrix is a function of the set of arrays it was given \
and of nothing else. Giving the same arrays in a different order produces the \
identical expression.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"00b2fc06-4dc5-1a44-98ea-2a0667f26752"],

Cell["\<\
An irregular array is necessarily \"Rigid\", since only a regular array can \
carry a symmetry, so the symmetry criterion separates the regular arrays \
among themselves.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c20eb613-adb5-e846-bb78-52d2d62e6298"],

Cell["\<\
Arrays of any kind of entry sit together freely. Raw entries given in place \
of an array are promoted to an ArrayObject.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"26e67b61-3d8a-234a-8000-ee0629516467"],

Cell["\<\
Length gives the number of arrays, and Normal the entries of each of them in \
order.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2f739d41-46ec-a446-8477-5ecb45f545f2"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"0442afc0-88b6-4d4c-b620-d024fed2a39d"],

Cell["The arrays are sorted whatever order they are given in:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"d8981830-b512-8142-97af-3338f098a286"],

Cell["\<\
hm = Hypermatrix[{
   ArrayObject[Array[1 &, {2, 2, 2}], \"Symmetric\"],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}],
   ArrayObject[{1, 2}],
   ArrayObject[{1, 2, 3}],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, \"Symmetric\"],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, \"Cyclic\"]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c5b32094-73d9-0c46-b359-438cefefd336"],

